  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "associated-oyster-3ec6",
  "summary": "New RNA tools span siRNA activity, translation efficiency, tRNA nanopore classification and oligo MS, pointing to maturing design and measurement for RNA therapeutics.",
  "synthesis": "The current items center on RNA-focused computational methods that predict or measure molecular behavior from sequence or signal, rather than on cell-type-resolved omics databases. DeepRNAi predicts on- and off-target siRNA knockdown and releases a benchmark dataset. A translation efficiency model adds protein language model amino acid embeddings to mRNA-derived features. A nanopore classifier assigns E. coli tRNA species from raw ionic currents without basecalling, at 98.2% accuracy. OligoFragger uses spectrum graphs to constrain modified-oligonucleotide MS/MS searches with FDR control. BIOREDIS integrates nine resources for codon optimization and shRNA/siRNA design. The new contributions are mainly feature enrichment, benchmarking, signal-level classification and workflow integration; the items do not show head-to-head comparisons across these tools.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
